seg-0c6f5e26367f = FFT (fast Fourier transform) acquisition of one or more PRNs (pseudo-random noise codes) over a recording (<c1/>), optionally behind front-end stages: per PRN, acquired or not, Doppler, code phase, peak statistic and threshold; <c2/> (one PRN) keeps the whole Doppler × code-phase correlation surface with fine-Doppler refinements.

